 SPIKE ONLY. THROWAWAY. How a still frame goes out as text, for
 harness/spike_svg.py to turn into a picture. Nothing grades this.

 A CHAPTER OF ITS OWN BECAUSE THERE ARE TWO ENTRIES NOW, and one of them cannot
 simply cite the other: a bundle is ONE FLAT NAMESPACE (PORTING_NOTES B5), so
 SpikeTruckMain citing SpikeMain for `all-cmds` collided on `opening` --
 "CDX3001 Duplicate definition: opening" -- which is the namespace rule doing
 exactly what it says. The printing moves here, both entries cite it, and neither
 restates it.

 COORDINATES GO OUT AS SCALED INTEGERS because `show` on a Real is still refused
 by the zig plug -- it needs a __real_to_text it does not have. real-to-int landed
 in 2026-08-29's plug work, so hundredths of a pixel is a plain multiply and a
 truncation, and a hundredth of a pixel is far finer than anything an SVG viewed
 at 960 by 600 can show.

 ONE LINE FOR THE WHOLE FRAME, commands separated by semicolons, rather than a
 print per command. A Codex `act` has no recursive loop shape, and a chapter is
 not the place to discover one for a throwaway: building the text purely and
 handing it to a single print is the boring option and it is fine here, because a
 frame is about a hundred kilobytes of digits.

   C <tag> <colour> <strength e-3> <n> <x e-2> <y e-2> ... [<colour2> <geom e-2>...]

 We say:

Section: Printing

  scaled : Real -> Text
  scaled (v) = show (real-to-int (v * 100.0))

  coords : List Real, Integer -> Text
  coords (ps) (i) =
    if i >= list-length ps then ""
    else " " & scaled (list-at ps i) & coords ps (i + 1)

 THE GRADIENT TAGS TRAIL THEIR EXTRAS, so a tag 0 or 1 line is byte-identical to
 what this printed before them and the reader needs no new rule for the common
 case. A tag 4, 5 or 6 line carries its second colour and then its own geometry
 AFTER the polygon: the reader knows from the tag how many numbers to expect and
 the point count already told it where the polygon ended.

  extras : DrawCmd -> Text
  extras (c) =
    if c.tag >= 4 then " " & show c.color2 & coords c.geom 0 else ""

  cmd-line : DrawCmd -> Text
  cmd-line (c) =
    "C " & show c.tag & " " & show c.color & " " & show (real-to-int (c.strength * 1000.0)) & " " & show (list-length c.pts / 2) & coords c.pts 0 & extras c

  all-cmds : List DrawCmd, Integer -> Text
  all-cmds (cs) (i) =
    if i >= list-length cs then ""
    else cmd-line (list-at cs i) & " ; " & all-cmds cs (i + 1)

 One SCENE header per viewpoint, and it carries the sky and horizon colours too,
 because blitter.js paints those itself from the module's numbers and an SVG has
 to do the same or the frame floats on nothing.

  scene-line : Text, Real -> Text
  scene-line (name) (u) =
    "SCENE " & name & " " & show (sky-color (scene-step-at u)) & " " & show (horizon-color (scene-step-at u))
